  "name": "Tone stack · Baxandall (bass, mid, treble)",
  "version": {
    "major": 1,
    "minor": 2
  },
  "description": "An active Baxandall tone control with a third, Mid, control: Bass, Mid (around 1 kHz) and Treble, each about ±20 dB, flat with every knob half-way. Values from Texas Instruments' TL082-N data sheet (SNOSBW5C), Figure 28 \"Three-Band Active Tone Control\" (TI's drawing has no refs; ours run left to right); all pots linear, as TI says. A TL071 for the TL082's half, on 9 V with + at vref instead of ±15 V and ground. Left out: TI's input buffer (a TL082 follower with 5 µF in and 10k to ground); C5, TI's 1 µF after it, is kept. It needs a low-impedance source: inside an effect, an op-amp output or an emitter or source follower before it is enough; from the guitar, a pot or a transistor's collector, put a buffer first (Buffer · op-amp (Klon)). The output sits at vref. Wire vref to a Vref divider.",
  "tags": [
    "tone",
    "tone stack",
    "opamp",
    "baxandall"
  ],
