  "notes": {
    "part:VR1": "Bass: clockwise boosts (to about +20 dB at the bottom of the range), anticlockwise cuts, half-way is flat. C1 bridges the pot, so the treble goes round it.",
    "part:VR2": "Mid: clockwise boosts a band around 1 kHz (to about +20 dB), anticlockwise cuts it, half-way is flat. C2 and C3 set the band.",
    "part:VR3": "Treble: clockwise boosts, anticlockwise cuts, half-way is flat. C4 lets only the treble reach the op-amp from it.",
    "part:C1": "47n, the standard value; TI's original has 0.05 µF (50n) here.",
    "part:IC1": "The three networks sit in this op-amp's feedback, so cut and boost are symmetrical and flat loses nothing. It inverts the signal."
  }
